    "template": "introspection/modulation prompts wrap the vendored contents in the repo's chat convention (USER:/ASSISTANT:, x13's PROMPT_TEMPLATE family); assistant turns are separated by the eos token (the literal '</s>' piece becomes tokenizer.eos_token_id when the tokenizer has one); vendored content strings are used verbatim",
    "spans": "the intro prompt is assembled from the vendored turns; user-turn spans (both user messages) are the injection positions, the intermediate assistant turn (' Understood.') is the position control; segments are tokenized per piece and concatenated so spans are exact by construction (BOS prepended once, matching the processor path's add_bos_token)",
    "strength": "injection strength k scales the raw vector to a fraction of the edited span's mean residual norm per layer: alpha_l = k * mean(||h_l|| over the span) / ||v_t,l|| (the x7 add convention, so 'add' alphas are comparable across layers/concepts)",
    "match": "concept-reported = word-boundary regex match of the concept's surface form in the generated completion (the fixed prefill is part of the prompt, not the response)",
